From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:07:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx: don't wake
 from USB

Every exit from CX power collapse in s2idle puts an edge on the armed
DP/DM HS-PHY wake lines of the USB controllers, so with USB wakeup
enabled the laptop wakes again a few seconds into every suspend. The
firmware does not use USB as a wake source on this machine either.

Drop wakeup-source from the four USB controllers in use; dwc3 then
powers the cores down across system suspend. An external USB keyboard
can no longer wake the laptop; the internal keyboard, the lid and the
power key still do.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
index fbbf1d9b940d..7af48732f7f0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
@@ -961,6 +961,8 @@ bluetooth {
 };
 
 &usb_0 {
+	/delete-property/ wakeup-source;
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -990,6 +992,8 @@ &usb_0_qmpphy_out {
 };
 
 &usb_1 {
+	/delete-property/ wakeup-source;
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -1019,6 +1023,8 @@ &usb_1_qmpphy_out {
 };
 
 &usb_2 {
+	/delete-property/ wakeup-source;
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -1048,6 +1054,8 @@ &usb_2_qmpphy_out {
 };
 
 &usb_hs {
+	/delete-property/ wakeup-source;
+
 	dr_mode = "host";
 
 	status = "okay";
